Package Update Test Suite

Package Update Test Suite is framework for testing of package install/update.
This test suite virifies whether PackageManagerService can manage installed applications and
user data correctly through SW update (ROM1 -> ROM2).

Background:
- PackageManagerService is huge and complicated.
- Bugs in PackageManagerService cause serious problems on market.
- To maintain PackageManagerService securely, automated test is thought to be needed.

How to use it:

[Prerequisite]
- Ubuntu PC is required.
  (Test execution has been verified on Ubuntu14.)
- Pixel / Pixel 2 are available with bootloader unlocked fully.
- Latest fastboot
- Latest Android SDK / NDK
- Download ROM images
  Need to place 2 version ROM for simulating letter update
  ex:ROM
      + -- radio.img
      + -- bootloader.img
      + -- aosp_walleye-img-xxxx-zip

[Create test applications]
1. $ cd frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/app-generate
2. $ export SDK_ROOT=<path/to/sdk>
3. $ export NDK_ROOT=<path/to/ndk>
4. $ app-genrerate.bash
5. When it is succeeded in building test applications, below directory and applications are created.

        app-generate
        +-- results
        |   +-- com.android.tests.pkgup001
        |   |   +-- ver1
        |   |   |   +-- TestApp001.apk
        |   |   |   +-- libs
        |   |   |       +-- arm64-v8a
        |   |   |       |   +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   |       +-- armeabi
        |   |   |       |   +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   |       +-- armeabi-v7a
        |   |   |           +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   +-- ver10
        |   |   |   +-- TestApp001.apk
        |   |   |   +-- libs
        |   |   |       +-- arm64-v8a
        |   |   |       |   +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   |       +-- armeabi
        |   |   |       |   +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   |       +-- armeabi-v7a
        |   |   |           +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   +-- ver2
        |   |   |   +-- TestApp001.apk
        |   |   |   +-- libs
        |   |   |       +-- arm64-v8a
        |   |   |       |   +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   |       +-- armeabi
        |   |   |       |   +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   |       +-- armeabi-v7a
        |   |   |           +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   +-- ver3
        |   |   |   +-- TestApp001.apk
        |   |   |   +-- libs
        |   |   |       +-- arm64-v8a
        |   |   |       |   +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   |       +-- armeabi
        |   |   |       |   +-- libTestApp001.so
        |   |   |       +-- armeabi-v7a
        |   |   |           +-- libTestApp001.so


6. Compress the test applications
   $ cd results/
   $ zip -r testapps.zip ./


[Run test]
1. $ cd frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate
2. $ bash run_test.bash -s <ANDROID_SERIAL> -r testcases/01_basic-scope/o2o/ testcases/01_basic-scope/testcase.txt <path/to/the/test_apps> <path/to/the/rom_1st> <path/to/the/rom_2nd>

ex) $ bash run_test.bash -s XXXXXXX -r testcases/01_basic-scope/o2o/ testcases/01_basic-scope/testcase.txt app-generate/results/testapps.zip ROM/ROM1.zip ROM/ROM2.zip

- ANDROID_SERIAL: You can get info with below commands
  $ adb devices
- ROM1/ROM2.zip
  ex:ROM1
      + -- radio.img
      + -- bootloader.img
      + -- aosp_walleye-img-xxxx-zip

3. If you are required to input sudo password, please input.
4. When all tests are executed, whole results are placed in frameworks/base/tests/PackageUpdate/reports/
   reports/html/analysis.html are available.


Appendix:
This test script uses ext2simg and related libraries in order to compose test images.
These binaries in tools/ were made by full-build results of android-8.1.0_r5

tools/
+ ext2simg
+--lib64
|   +-- libbase.so
|   +-- libc++.so
|   +-- libext2_com_err-host.so
|   +-- libext2fs-host.so
|   +-- liblog.so
|   +-- libsparse-host.so
|   +-- libz-host.so
+ simg2img
